# MimOS's own preset policy.
#
# It exists to say one thing: MimOS manages the network with NetworkManager,
# so systemd-networkd is disabled by policy. Without this file the policy is
# only implied -- MimOS masks those units -- and systemd's own
# 90-systemd.preset says `enable systemd-networkd.service`, which is a
# contradiction the first boot resolves by printing an error at everybody.
#
#     Failed to preset all unit: Unit /etc/systemd/system/\
#     systemd-networkd.service is masked
#
# Two of those, in red, on the Live screen every single boot. Measured on
# David's ASUS on 2026-08-10 and reproduced verbatim offline against systemd
# 261 with `systemctl --root=`. See ADR-135 for the two repairs that were
# tried first and failed, including moving the mask to /usr/lib.
#
# 10 rather than 50 or 90: presets are read in lexicographic order across the
# whole search path and the first matching line wins, so this must sort above
# systemd's own 90-systemd.preset.
#
# This changes nothing on a machine that is already up. PID 1 applies presets
# only on a first boot -- one with no /etc/machine-id -- and Arch runs no
# preset hook on package installation. On an installed MimOS, Calamares writes
# the machine-id before the first boot, so the only system that ever reads
# this file is the Live one, where every boot is a first boot.

disable systemd-networkd.service
disable systemd-networkd.socket
disable systemd-networkd-wait-online.service
disable dbus-org.freedesktop.network1.service
